4:    World integration contract (js/world.js is not present in this
5:    checkout):
6:    - Call Battle.start({ type:'wild', party, wild:{ species, level }, ... })
7:      or Battle.start({ type:'trainer', party, trainerId, ... }).
8:    - party is the live array of member objects: { species (or id), level,
9:      hp, maxHp, moves:[moveId,...], status?, xp? }. Missing combat fields
10:      are initialized in place; battle changes (HP, status, XP, evolution,
11:      captured team members, money) remain on the supplied objects/arrays.
12:    - Optional args: inventory (quantity map), player (object with money),
13:      trainer (trainer data object), `teamBattle:true` for two active Pokémon
14:      per side, and onEnd(result). Trainer teams are sent out sequentially.
15:      The returned session has `finished` and a promise that resolves to the
16:      final result. A wild encounter may also pass `canRun:false` or
17:      `canCapture:false`.
18:    - The global Battle API also exposes createMember(species, level, opts),
